• Algorithm

Step 1: Start

Step 2: Define a Node structure to hold vehicle number, owner name, and a pointer to the next vehicle.

Step 3: Show menu options continuously: Add, Display, Search, Remove, and exit.

Step 4: Check full status during insertion; if currentCount == MAX_CAPACITY, display "Parking full" and stop.

Step 5: Add vehicle by creating a new node at the end of the list and increasing currentCount by 1.

Step 6: Display list by traveling from head to the end, printing all vehicle numbers and names.

Step 7: Search vehicle by matching the user's input number with each node sequentially.

Step 8: Locate target node and its previous node when removing a vehicle from parking.

Step 9: Remove vehicle by changing pointers to bypass the target node, freeing memory, and decreasing currentCount by 1.

Step 10: Exit and stop program execution when the user chooses option 5.
